  "pull_request": {
    "number": 127,
    "title": "Provide fallback to powershell if pwsh is not present when bootstrapping",
    "body": "When bootstrapping using `cargo xtask bootstrap` on Windows without a separately installed `pwsh`, the bootstrapping process will fail because of \"program not found\".\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces a function `get_powershell_command` that chooses the appropriate PowerShell command on Windows. It defaults to `pwsh` and falls back to `powershell` if `pwsh` is not present.\r\n\r\nThe bootstrapping process had been tested with both shells.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">When bootstrapping using <code class=\"notranslate\">cargo xtask bootstrap</code> on Windows without a separately installed <code class=\"notranslate\">pwsh</code>, the bootstrapping process will fail because of \"program not found\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR introduces a function <code class=\"notranslate\">get_powershell_command</code> that chooses the appropriate PowerShell command on Windows. It defaults to <code class=\"notranslate\">pwsh</code> and falls back to <code class=\"notranslate\">powershell</code> if <code class=\"notranslate\">pwsh</code> is not present.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The bootstrapping process had been tested with both shells.</p>",
